    {
      "action": "create",
      "nodeId": "triangle-midpoints/equal-area-program",
      "parentId": "root",
      "nodeType": "program",
      "title": "Triangle-midpoint area structure",
      "summary": "This program studies the geometric and affine consequences of taking D, E, and F as the side midpoints of a nondegenerate triangle ABC. Established knowledge includes the midpoint-segment relations, quarter-area results for the medial and corner triangles, half-scaling of the relevant corner altitudes, and equality of all four small areas. Formal verification remains prospective, and there is no supplied active mathematical dispute.",
